  "problem": "$\\text{curl}\\,F\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\u27e8$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=\u2207\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x} & \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y} & \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x} & \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y} & \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z} \\\\ {z}^{2} & 2xy & x{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(x{y}^{2})-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}(2xy)]i-[\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x{y}^{2})-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}({z}^{2})]j+[\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(2xy)-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({z}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(2xy-0)\\,i-({y}^{2}-2z)\\,j+(2y-0)\\,k \\\\  & =2xy\\,i-({y}^{2}-2z)\\,j+2y\\,k \\\\  & =\u27e82xy,\\,2z-{y}^{2},\\,2y\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
